# Per-finding exceptions, pinned to an exact commit, file, rule and line.
#
# This is the mechanism to reach for — never a path allowlist in .gitleaks.toml, which covers
# everything anyone adds to that file afterwards. A fingerprint stops being valid the moment the
# line moves, so it cannot silently widen.
#
# **Fingerprints are commit-pinned, so rebasing invalidates them.** These were written against the
# branch SHAs and every one broke the moment the PR was rebase-merged, turning `main` red. Land
# anything carrying a fingerprint with a **squash** merge, or repin immediately after. That trade —
# precision at the cost of surviving a rewrite — is the price of not using a path allowlist.
